# Spin Hobby server: the settings file for an intern's computer. SAFE TO SHARE: it holds no keys at all.
#
#   cp .env.intern .env
#   npm run dev:local
#
# The REQUIRED part below is all you need. With it the whole shop runs on your computer: a built-in test database (reset at
# every start), test sign-ins (owner@spinhobby.test / spinhobby, staff@spinhobby.test / spinhobby), sample products, the admin,
# and checkout with a TEST PAYMENT (no card, no money). Each OPTIONAL part turns on one more thing, with keys you make yourself
# (never the shop's real ones). Leave a part empty and that feature is simply off: nothing else breaks.
#
# Safety, whatever ends up in this file: `npm run dev:local` never uses the shop's databases (it refuses them), leaves out live Square,
# live PayPal and production eBay keys (it says so when it starts), and stops the paid AI tool at $5 a month. Never commit or paste your .env.

# ============================================================================================ REQUIRED (filled in: keep as is)

NODE_ENV=development
# Any Square, PayPal or eBay keys you add below must be TEST (sandbox) ones: these three lines say so, and the local start checks.
SQUARE_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox
PAYPAL_ENV=sandbox
EBAY_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox

# ============================================================================================ OPTIONAL (empty = that feature is off)

# ---- Your own database: keeps your data between runs (the built-in one starts fresh every time). A free Supabase project:
# supabase.com → New project (save the database password) → Connect → "Session pooler" → copy the URI and put your password in it.
# The first `npm run dev:local` sets it up (every migration + the sample shop); `npm run dev:local -- --reset` reloads the samples.
# DEV_DATABASE_URL=

# ---- Square sandbox: your own test Square shop. Turns on: its catalog synced in, card checkout with Square's test cards
# (4111 1111 1111 1111), creating products in Square from the admin and from Gleamshelf drafts.
# Without it: products you add are kept in our database only, and checkout uses the test payment.
# Free: developer.squareup.com → sign up → Create an application → "Sandbox" at the top → Credentials and Locations.
# SQUARE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# SQUARE_APPLICATION_ID=
# SQUARE_LOCATION_ID=

# ---- PayPal sandbox: checkout with a PayPal test buyer. Without it: the test payment (or Square, if set above).
# Free: developer.paypal.com → Apps & Credentials → "Sandbox" → Create App.
# PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
# PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ---- eBay sandbox: connect a test eBay seller and list from the admin (docs/EBAY.md). Without it: Settings → eBay says "not set up".
# Free: developer.ebay.com → Hire an application keyset (Sandbox). EBAY_TOKEN_KEY: run `openssl rand -base64 32`.
# EBAY_CLIENT_ID=
# EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET=
# EBAY_RU_NAME=
# EBAY_TOKEN_KEY=

# ---- Email: order confirmation emails. Without it: no email is sent, the order still completes.
# Careful: this sends REAL email. Use your own Resend account (resend.com, free tier) and only order with your own address.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# FROM_EMAIL=

# ---- Paid AI: the cashier's "photo to listing" tool (Anthropic). Every photo costs real money. Without it: the tool says it is off.
# Only with a key the shop owner made for you, with its own spending limit. Never use someone else's key.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
